  "id": "personal-construct-therapy",
  "term": "personal construct therapy",
  "definition": "Personal construct therapy is a psychological approach that focuses on how a person makes sense of themselves and their experiences. Rather than teaching about depression or directing specific changes in thoughts or behaviour, it explores whether the person’s thoughts and actions fit with their sense of identity and looks at the meanings they give to these experiences.",
